ORIGIN OF THE MATERIAL

Every sample in this corpus was authored in the powershell-lsp repository. A
per-file provenance audit of the corpus surface -- first-add commit, content
marker sweep, upstream comparison, and commit-trailer scan -- found zero files
derived from an external source and zero of unknown origin. There is no
third-party rightsholder anywhere in the sample surface. See PROVENANCE.md in
this directory for the audit, its instruments, and the limits each instrument
carries.

THIRD-PARTY CONTENT

This package contains no third-party content.

The powershell-lsp repository does carry one vendored third-party file -- the
OASIS SARIF 2.1.0 JSON Schema at tests/sarif/sarif-2.1.0.json, under the OASIS
IPR Policy (RF on RAND Terms Mode), not under Apache-2.0. It is a test fixture
for validating SARIF output and is NOT part of this corpus package. It is named
here only so that "no third-party content" above is a checked statement rather
than an assumed one.

The two runtime components powershell-lsp depends on (PowerShell Editor Services
and PSScriptAnalyzer, both Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation, MIT) are
downloaded at install time by the plugin and are likewise not part of this
package.
